"The whole system of magic is the life's work of the goddess called Mother, Mother of Magic."
"Magic skills are a scaffold for the unskilled; raw magic can rebuild any skill by hand."
"Skill Deconstruct, a gift of the gods, breaks a skill to reveal its construct template."
"Deconstructing a magic skill reveals part of its governing symbol, the key to its branch."
"A god warns that those who dig beneath magic's surface usually end up killing themselves."
"Mana Dominion can be reached only with the approval of a divine power."
"Reaching Mana Dominion earns a Legend Point, for reaching the pinnacle of mana."
"Elemental Shift hides a secret: an affinity can be pushed past its limit, even faked."
"Chaos magic cores at least double chaos output, as if making those affinities official."
"Elemental Praxis is a hidden skill that measures mastery of the whole elemental system."
"Spells woven from the system's own interface feel eldritch; onlookers feel primal dread."
"The goddess of magic quietly discounts magic skills for those she favours."
"Rumour holds that Legend Points can buy rare affinities, skills and traits."
